* 3-phase BLDC generator subcircuit
* W input:     1 V = 1 mechanical rad/s
* TGEN output: 1 V = 1 N·m generator braking torque

.subckt BLDCGEN A B C W TGEN 

.func trap(x) {limit((3/pi)*asin(sin(x)),-1,1)}

* Generated phase back-EMFs
BEMFA EA N V={Ke*V(W)*trap(idt(pp*V(W),0))}
BEMFB EB N V={Ke*V(W)*trap(idt(pp*V(W),0)-2*pi/3)}
BEMFC EC N V={Ke*V(W)*trap(idt(pp*V(W),0)+2*pi/3)}

* Phase winding resistance and inductance
RA EA LA {Rs}
LA LA A  {Ls}

RB EB LB {Rs}
LB LB B  {Ls}

RC EC LC {Rs}
LC LC C  {Ls}

* Numerical reference for the internal neutral
RREF N 0 1G

* Generator torque output: 1 V = 1 N·m
BTGEN TGEN 0 V={(V(EA,N)*I(RA)+V(EB,N)*I(RB)+V(EC,N)*I(RC))/V(W)}

.ends BLDCGEN